WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
<v Narrator>The same invitation can land very differently on two people in the same room.

2
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:11.350
A senior employee and someone in their first month may both hear, “Any questions?”

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.300
Their position and their past experience differ, so the risk feels different.

4
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.050
The readings name several things that shape that risk.

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.400
Position.

6
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.550
How earlier questions were received.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.700
How visible the person is.

8
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.850
What support they can reach.

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
None of that creates a rule about any one person.

10
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:37.350
It does mean you should not read someone's confidence, experience or agreement from

11
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.700
silence alone.

12
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:44.450
And repeatedly asking the least secure person to be braver can leave the real

13
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.800
conditions unchanged.

14
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.750
<v Narrator>Many leaders say their door is always open.

15
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.900
That statement helps only when what happens next supports it.

16
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:58.450
The person who invites input may also control assignments, evaluations and

17
00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.800
development.

18
00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.150
Staff can reasonably weigh those consequences before disagreeing.

19
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:09.300
In one reading's practice case, a temporary staff member sees an access problem in a

20
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.650
form.

21
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.000
She expects that challenging the project lead in public could harm her future

22
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:17.350
assignments.

23
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.300
A prepared written route, or a private conversation, may make that contribution

24
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:23.650
usable.

25
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.800
It should not require her to explain her personal history.

26
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:34.350
And a lack of visitors through the open door does not show that no concerns exist.

27
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.700
<v Narrator>The Fearless Organization reading adds a point about inclusion.

28
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:43.650
Staff from underrepresented groups often bear the highest cost for speaking up.

29
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.200
So a climate that punishes candor tends to silence them first.

30
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.150
The same reading notes a common critique.

31
00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:56.500
Edmondson's framework says little about how power and identity shape who feels safe.

32
00:01:56.650 --> 00:02:01.450
Her later writing addresses this, the reading notes, but practitioners should still

33
00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.200
add an equity lens.

34
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.950
Here is the guardrail.

35
00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:10.700
This is about conditions on a team, not about what any one person feels.

36
00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:15.250
You cannot know someone's experience from a group they belong to.

37
00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:20.200
The reading asks whether people from different identity groups experience the same

38
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:25.150
level of safety on your team, and how you would find out.

39
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.300
Finding out is the point.

40
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.650
Guessing is not.

41
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:34.200
<v Narrator>One reading tells a practice story about two colleagues reviewing a draft.

42
00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:38.750
One asks questions right away, as the draft is read aloud.

43
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:44.100
The other wants to review the wording first and send a prepared question.

44
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.650
At first, each misreads the other.

45
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.600
The quick questioner sees the delay as reluctance to challenge the team.

46
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:56.950
The careful preparer sees the quick questions as putting colleagues on the spot.

47
00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.700
Then each explains what their habit means to them.

48
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:06.850
For one, asking right away showed care: you name a problem while others can still

49
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.200
fix it together.

50
00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:12.750
For the other, arriving with a considered question respected everyone's preparation

51
00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.100
and the relationship.

52
00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.250
Both cared about the work.

53
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.200
Those meanings belonged to those two people, who chose to share them.

54
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.750
Neither one speaks for a group.

55
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:29.700
<v Narrator>The lesson is not to list styles or ask people to be tolerant.

56
00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.650
It is to change what you do.

57
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.800
Make the open question visible.

58
00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:41.350
Let people raise it in the room, or send a prepared question in time for the

59
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.700
decision.

60
00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:48.050
Then check that the written route actually reaches the person responsible before the

61
00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.400
choice closes.

62
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:53.550
A comment box nobody reads is not a real option.

63
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:59.300
Moving someone's contribution out of the room and then forgetting it keeps the look

64
00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.850
of choice while losing the knowledge.

65
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.200
Privately, notice which signal you tend to reward.

66
00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:06.550
Speed.

67
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.900
Certainty.

68
00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:09.250
Preparation.

69
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.600
Direct challenge.

70
00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.950
Each one can be a form of care.

71
00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:15.900
<v Narrator>One more guardrail.

72
00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:22.050
A person should not have to share a personal history, or explain an experience of

73
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.000
exclusion, before their question is taken seriously.

74
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:31.950
Nor should anyone be asked to speak for a whole community, or to carry the work of

75
00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.900
educating others because of who they are.

76
00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:40.650
A practical concern about a form or a process can stand on its own.

77
00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.000
Ask for evidence and perspective, not identity stories.

78
00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:50.150
If someone chooses to share more, receive it with care and keep it with them.

